tances can emit different conventions in the same JVM.\n\nFor 3.0, remove global-backed RPC factories and the no-argument RPC/service-peer selection helpers. Pass the instrumentation's `OpenTelemetry` instance instead:\n\n```diff\n-RpcClientMetrics.get()\n+RpcClientMetrics.get(openTelemetry)\n-RpcSpanNameExtractor.create(getter)\n+RpcSpanNameExtractor.create(getter, openTelemetry)\n-SemconvStability.emitOldRpcSemconv()\n+SemconvStability.emitOldRpcSemconv(openTelemetry)\n```\n\nThe client/server attribute extractors, server metrics, dual-emission context customizer, remaining RPC/service-peer selection helpers, and `rpcSchemaUrl` likewise require an explicit instance.\n\nRPC consumers pass their own instance, and AWS RPC extractors are instance-owned. Span names, attributes, metrics, and schema URLs follow the same selection. Legacy child metrics no longer inherit a dual-emitting parent's method.\n\nDatabase, messaging, and code conventions remain unchanged.\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n- Fixes #20135","title":"Make semantic convention selection OpenTelemetry instance-scoped"},"mode":"publish","pr":20474,"pr_author_id":198982749,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1791600631,"generation":4,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"d4d4075e871a418e8f59e51d2db4d642","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":[]},"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","repo_id":210933087,"request_id":"21d6eda979bf49c389732e1ef8c19e93","schema":2,"source_private":false,"target_private":false,"workflow_ref":"review-loop-revisions/36edb5cc3e04fa082cd2e4dd199c7036d365a000","workflow_revision":"36edb5cc3e04fa082cd2e4dd199c7036d365a000"},"run":{"attempt":1,"conclusion":"success","id":38018448517,"url":"https://github.com/trask/copilot-workflows/actions/runs/38018448517"},"schema":2,"seen_findings":[],"seen_inline_findings":[],"seen_missed_findings":[],"stage":"publication_intent"